    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}-4t,\\,y=2{t}^{3}+21{t}^{2}+72t,\\,-\\infty<t<\\infty.\n$$\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is horizontal. Give exact answers.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the tangent to the curve is horizontal at $t=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $t=$\n{{field-2}}.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/value": "-4",
